From e65cb0f46ce6480a378a22b7e4953d5c3220a5e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:47:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] local: full travel on open/close, stored positions on the
 tilt buttons

For the Raffstore motors a HA tilt click sent a single short-press byte
(0x20/0x40), which only nudges the slats, and close sent 0x44, which ends
with the slats restored open. Map Home Assistant instead to:

  open        0x21  full up
  close       0x41  full down, slats stay closed
  tilt open   0x24  saved tilt / ventilation position (remote: 2x up)
  tilt close  0x44  saved intermediate position (remote: 2x down)

DOWN is now 0x41; the 0x44 constant is renamed INTERMEDIATE, which the
web UI "int" action keeps sending. The single-step bytes stay available
as TILT_UP/TILT_DOWN.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019Jt9MRmy72MEcuogzanZQE
